From f84b36e7a816e1695aa2b13ede822251ee5ff49a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:35:31 +1000
Subject: [PATCH v2 2/4] ui/spice: send each damaged region as one DRAW_COPY

qemu_spice_create_update() diffs the damage against the mirror surface
in 32 pixel wide columns and emits one QXL_DRAW_COPY per run of changed
rows in each column. A 480x360 region that changes every frame thus
reaches the spice server as fifteen or more 32 pixel wide draws per
update, and more when some rows of a column happen not to change.

That defeats the spice server's video stream detection. With
streaming-video=filter each 32x360 column passes the minimum area check
on its own, so the server starts one 32 pixel wide stream per column,
while columns whose runs are broken by unchanged rows never stream and
keep being sent as lossless images. With a Linux guest playing a
480x360 video at 30 fps on virtio-vga, spice-server 0.15.2 started 18
streams and the display channel carried 27 MB in 28 seconds.

Use the mirror diff only to shrink each damage rectangle to the
bounding box of the pixels that changed, split it where at least 32
rows are unchanged, drop it if nothing changed, and send each box as
a single DRAW_COPY. Damage that repeats every frame then produces a
steady run of identically sized draws, which the server turns into a
single stream: in the same test, one 480x360 stream and 5 MB. The row
split matters because guests often report far more damage than what
changed: Linux virtio-gpu flushes the whole plane, VGA whole scanlines.

The diff is in the unit tested helper. It narrows down differences
with memcmp() and only examines the parts of each row outside the box
found so far, so it costs about one memcmp() pass over the damage; on
a 1920x1080 frame that is as fast or faster than the column diff for
every change pattern measured, and much faster when everything changed.

Prompt: Harden the spice damage prototype toward upstream: unit test
the diff, benchmark its worst case against the old column diff at
1920x1080 and optimise it if it is slower, and keep each patch
checkpatch clean and bisectable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, low effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
